WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:14.536
A staged rollout reduces the risk of releasing to the whole
fleet at once. Start with a small test set, observe the results,
then expand in groups. Use this when a bad release could disrupt
many devices or customer sites.

2
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:27.144
Open Create a gradual rollout and enter the release details
shown here. These identify the software and installation
instructions that each device must verify before applying the
update.

3
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:39.464
List the device sets in the order you want to update them. The
interface calls these cohorts. Put your pilot devices first,
then add larger sets after you have evidence that the release is
working.

4
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:53.896
Set how quickly devices are admitted, how long each set should
be observed and how many failures should stop progress. The
observation time is called the bake period. Choose values that
allow meaningful health reports to arrive.

5
00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:08.488
Creating the rollout does not immediately admit devices. Select
it and choose Check device health and continue to evaluate the
next admission. This gives you a controlled point to review
health before more devices start.

6
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:23.557
Watch the reported results as you proceed. Pause or abort to
stop further admissions if there is a problem. A device that has
already started an installation may finish; these controls do
not automatically undo an update.

